Subject: [PATCH 27/47] inkling2: tf_ik_attention_flash keeps its output
 accumulators in registers (the epilogue's row loop unrolled; o was a 272-byte
 stack array), stages each tile's relative bias rows in shared memory with its
 keys, and skips the per-score mask on tiles 1024 or more behind a warp's rows
 (same scores in the same order, bits unchanged)

---
 zig/kernels/cuda/inkling2_attention_flash.cuh | 44 +++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 35 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/zig/kernels/cuda/inkling2_attention_flash.cuh b/zig/kernels/cuda/inkling2_attention_flash.cuh
