From: LPFchan <me@lost.plus>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 03:14:51 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 41/47] inkling2: TF_INKLING_STREAMS (1 to 4, default 4) serves
 that many requests at once: each on a slot of its own (local rings, drafter
 state), the global caches' regions in one shared pool (pool.zig: first fit,
 idle kept turns evicted oldest first, then compaction; rank 0 places, both
 ranks run the moves, overlapping copies through the workspace), and the
 streams' draft verifies in one shared pass (Forward.verifyBatch, at most 8
 rows a stream, 24 in all). Every stream's replies are as when it runs alone;
 STREAMS=1 keeps one whole-context ring and today's bits. 1/2/4 streams:
 44.9/50.6/56.7 tok/s in all

