From 45d420bbdfa073b67c50f12dc226ecda46b0c2dd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LPFchan <me@lost.plus>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 06:43:55 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 47/47] inkling2: unlimited images per request
 (--vision-max-images 0) with per-image token cap and lazy chunked encoding

Allow --vision-max-images 0 (unlimited) where --vision-image-tokens bounds each image individually instead of dividing a shared pool across all images in the conversation. Inkling 2 prepares image metadata lazily (with a 256-entry metadata cache so cached history skips PNG/JPEG/WebP decoding), plans image batches per prefill chunk into its reusable rows buffer (avoiding straddle re-encodes and sending dynamic span records to rank 1), lifts the 20 MB total image-bytes cap on chat routes (keeping 10 MB per image), and raises the HTTP request body cap to 256 MiB when unlimited images are enabled.
